 \\(0\\le k\\le n-3\\) is realizable.\n\n7. **Collecting the results.**  \n   Combining the lower bounds (at least two non‑sunny lines for \\(n\\ge4\\), at least three\n   for \\(n\\ge6\\)), the upper bounds (3) and (5), and the explicit constructions,\n   we obtain precisely the sets of admissible \\(k\\) listed in the statement of the\n   theorem. ∎"
